hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27395","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Idris, from Ibn Safwan, from Safiyya the Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will not cease attacking this House until an army attacks it, until when they are in a desert land, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed, and the middle of them will not escape. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what about the one coerced among them? He said: Allah will raise them according to what is in their hearts."
"27396","Sufyan said: Salama said: Ubayd ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to me, from Muslim, the like of this hadith."
"27397","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salama, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Idris, from Ibn Safwan, from Safiyya bint Huyayy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People will not cease attacking this House until when they are in a desert land, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed, and the middle of them will not escape. They said: O Messenger of Allah, among them will be the coerced. He said: Allah will raise them according to what is in their hearts."
"27398","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salama, from Abu Idris al-Murhibi, from Muslim ibn Safwan, from Safiyya, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will not cease, and he mentioned the hadith and narrated it."
"27399","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yala ibn Hakim, from Suhayra bint Jayfar, she said: I entered upon Safiyya bint Huyayy and asked about jar nabidh, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar nabidh."
"27400","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Safiyya bint Huyayy, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat, and I came to visit him at night and spoke with him, then I stood and turned back, so he stood with me to see me off. His dwelling was in the house of Usama ibn Zayd. Two men of the Ansar passed by, and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they hastened. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take your time, indeed she is Safiyya bint Huyayy. They said: Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Satan runs in man like the running of blood, and I feared he would cast evil, or he said something, into your hearts."
"27401","Wahb ibn Jarir said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Yala ibn Hakam narrating from Suhayrah bint Jayfar, she said: We performed Hajj, then we came to Madinah and entered upon Safiyyah bint Huyayy, and we found women with her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar."
"27402","Affan said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Hakim narrated to me from Suhayrah bint Jayfar, he heard it from her, she said: We performed Hajj, then we returned to Madinah and entered upon Safiyyah bint Huyayy, and we found women from Kufa with her, and they said to her: If you wish, you ask and we listen, and if you wish, we ask and you listen. So we said: Ask. So they asked about matters of a woman and her husband and about menstruation, then they asked about nabidh of the jar, and she said: You have asked us much, O people of Iraq, about nabidh of the jar; it is no burden on one of you to cook her dates, then mash them, then strain them, then put them in her waterskin and tie it, and when it becomes good, she drinks and gives her husband to drink."
"27403","Abd al-Razzaq said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Thabit, he said: Shumaysah - or Sumayyah; Abd al-Razzaq said: it is in my book Sumayyah - narrated to me from Safiyyah bint Huyayy, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj with his wives, and when he was partway, a man dismounted and drove them singing, and he went fast, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Like that is your driving of the glass vessels, meaning the women. And while they were traveling, the camel of Safiyyah bint Huyayy knelt, and she had among the best mounts, so she wept, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came when he was told of that and began wiping her tears with his hand, and she kept increasing in weeping while he forbade her; and when she did much, he rebuked her and scolded her and ordered the people to dismount, so they dismounted, though he had not intended to dismount. She said: So they dismounted, and it was my day; and when they dismounted, the tent of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pitched and he entered it. She said: I did not know why the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was displeased with me, and I feared there was something in himself against me, so I went to Aishah and said to her: You know I would never sell my day from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anything ever, and I have given my day to you on condition that you please the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward me. She said: Yes. He said: So Aishah took a khimar of hers that she had soaked with saffron and sprinkled it with water so its scent would be strong, then she wore her clothes, then she went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and lifted the edge of the tent, and he said to her: What is with you, O Aishah, this is not your day. She said: That is the bounty of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills. So he said: With your family. And when it was time to depart, he said to Zaynab bint Jahsh: O Zaynab, lend your sister Safiyyah a camel, and she had among the most mounts. So she said: Should I lend your Jewess? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry when he heard that from her, and he deserted her and did not speak to her until he came to Makkah, and the days of Mina in his journey, until he returned to Madinah, and Muharram and Safar, and he did not come to her nor allot for her, and she despaired of him. And when it was the month of Rabi al-Awwal, he entered upon her, and she saw his shadow and said: This is the shadow of a man, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does not enter upon me, so who is this? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and when she saw him she said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what to do when you entered upon me. She said: She had a slave girl and she used to hide her from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: So-and-so is yours. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to the bed of Zaynab, and it had been raised, so he put it down with his hand, then he went to his family and was pleased with them."
"27404","Affan said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us from Sumayyah from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and a camel of Safiyyah became ill, then he mentioned something similar."
